{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1452609-pre-made-characters-in-jumpstart-wrong-attributes","id":1452609,"title":"Pre-made Characters in Jumpstart: Wrong Attributes?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-17T04:29:42-07:00","id":1452609,"title":"Pre-made Characters in Jumpstart: Wrong Attributes?","content":"Hey guys, i'm a storyteller new to Changling the lost.<br /> I'm having my group working through the jumpstart scenario to get a first impression of how WOD works.<br /> <br /> But as per character creation rules in the core book, a changeling character gets 12+1 attribute points to spend in 9 attributes.<br /> And in contrast, those ready-made characters in jumpstart each have 14 or 15 points.<br /> <br /> BTW, it seems like they also have unspent merits.<br /> <br /> Is it intened to work like that, or should i cut the attribute total down to 13 points?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26901,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26901-flat-cat","user":"Flat Cat","date":". 06-17-2021, 07:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26901-flat-cat","name":"Flat Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T05:58:25-07:00","id":1452613,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s possible that the writers just wrote up reasonably acceptable starting-characters, not meticulously rule-proved ones, for sake of simplicity. <br /> <br /> From a practical point, having higher Attributes mean a boost to a broad category of dice pools, and having less Merits mean there being less complex mechanisms to crunch on; both nice for new players. So it\u2019s also possible that the \u2018wrong\u2019 numbers <i>could</i> have been intentional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T10:12:53-07:00","id":1452651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1452609-pre-made-characters-in-jumpstart-wrong-attributes?p=1452613#post1452613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s possible that the writers just wrote up reasonably acceptable starting-characters, not meticulously rule-proved ones, for sake of simplicity.<br /> <br /> From a practical point, having higher Attributes mean a boost to a broad category of dice pools, and having less Merits mean there being less complex mechanisms to crunch on; both nice for new players. So it\u2019s also possible that the \u2018wrong\u2019 numbers <i>could</i> have been intentional.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank a lot for your sharing.<br /> I and my players just literally went through every page, trying to find out if we ignored some rules that would provide extra Attributes.<br /> <br /> Now i can stop blaming myself for carelessness and finally find some inner peace.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26901-flat-cat","name":"Flat Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T07:32:27-07:00","id":1452953,"title":"","content":"I think they swapped Merit dots with Attributes using the xp cost as exchange rate.<br /> <br /> Looking at Ash, the Wisecracking Vizier:<br /> 14 Attribute dots instead of 13 =&gt; 1 extra dot = 4 xp cost<br /> <br /> Merits: Winter Mantle 2 <br /> 1 Mantle dot is free from Court<br /> <br /> 5 Merit dots spent for having Wyrd 2 at character creation, which leaves us with 5 Merit dots;<br /> 1 dot spent to increase Mantle from 1 to 2 dots<br /> <br /> The remaining 4 Merit dots are unspent, converted into xp at the 1 xp per dot rate =&gt; that's where the extra Attribute comes from.<br /> <br /> Haven't looked at the others but same logic should apply.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","name":"moonwhisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}